CASE 3: MICROSERVICES ARCHITECTURE WITH API GATEWAYS AND SERVICE-SPECIFIC LOAD BALANCERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose ek microservices architecture hai jisme multiple services hain.

Example:

    User Service
    Order Service
    Payment Service

Har service ke multiple instances different servers par run kar rahe hain.

Har service ke instances ko manage karne ke liye us service ka apna Load Balancer hai.

Example:

    User Service Load Balancer
    Order Service Load Balancer
    Payment Service Load Balancer


## WHAT PROBLEM DOES AN API GATEWAY SOLVE ?
--------------------------------------------

Suppose API Gateway nahi hai.

Architecture:

                           Client / User
                                |
      -------------------------------------------------------
      |                          |                          |
      |                          |                          |
      v                          v                          v
 user-service.company.com   order-service.company.com   payment-service.company.com
        (URL)                     (URL)                      (URL)
      |                          |                          |
      | DNS Resolution           | DNS Resolution           | DNS Resolution
      v                          v                          v
 User Service LB (IP)      Order Service LB (IP)      Payment Service LB (IP)
      |                          |                          |
      v                          v                          v
 User Instances            Order Instances           Payment Instances


Is architecture me client ko har service ke Load Balancer ka endpoint
(typically a URL / CNAME) maintain karna padega.

Har request ke time client us URL ka DNS Resolution
karke corresponding Load Balancer ka IP obtain karega.

Jaise-jaise microservices ki sankhya badhti jaati hai,
client ko aur bhi zyada service LB endpoints maintain karne padte hain.

Agar future me kisi service LB ka endpoint change ho jaye,
to client ko bhi update karna padega.

Iske alawa Authentication, Authorization, Rate Limiting,
Logging jaise common functionalities bhi har service me
alag-alag implement karni pad sakti hain.

Ye architecture maintain karna difficult ho jata hai.

Is problem ko solve karne ke liye API Gateway introduce kiya jata hai.

API Gateway client ke liye ek Single Entry Point provide karta hai.

Ab client ko sirf API Gateway ka endpoint / URL pata hona chahiye.

Baaki request ko kis service ke Load Balancer tak bhejna hai,
ye responsibility API Gateway ki hoti hai.


## WHAT EXACTLY IS AN API GATEWAY ?
------------------------------------

API Gateway koi physical hardware device nahi hota.

Ye ek software application hota hai jo client requests ke liye
Single Entry Point provide karta hai.
Ye khud bhi ek normal application ki tarah ek ya multiple
servers par run karta hai.

Examples:

    - Spring Cloud Gateway
    - Kong
    - NGINX
    - Traefik
    - Envoy
    - AWS API Gateway




## WHAT DOES AN API GATEWAY DO?
------------------------------------

API Gateway ka kaam sirf URL routing nahi hota.

Ye client aur microservices ke beech ek centralized layer ki
tarah kaam karta hai aur multiple common responsibilities
handle karta hai.

1. REQUEST ROUTING
-------------------

API Gateway incoming request ka URL check karta hai aur
request ko appropriate microservice ke Load Balancer tak
forward karta hai.

Example:

    /users/**      -> User Service Load Balancer

    /orders/**     -> Order Service Load Balancer

    /payments/**   -> Payment Service Load Balancer



2. AUTHENTICATION
------------------

API Gateway verify karta hai ki client authenticated hai ya nahi.

Example:

Client Request:

    GET /orders

Gateway validates the JWT token.

If the token is invalid or expired:

    401 Unauthorized

Request Order Service tak forward hi nahi hogi.


3. AUTHORIZATION
-----------------

Authentication ke baad Gateway verify karta hai ki user
requested resource access karne ke liye authorized hai ya nahi.

Example:

Client Request:

    DELETE /users/101

JWT Valid

Role = USER

DELETE operation sirf ADMIN perform kar sakta hai.

Result:

    403 Forbidden

Request User Service tak nahi jayegi.



4. RATE LIMITING
------------------

API Gateway excessive requests ko block karta hai taaki
backend services overload na ho.

Example:

Allowed:

    100 requests/minute

Attacker sends:

    100000 requests/second

Gateway Response:

    429 Too Many Requests

Backend service unnecessary load se bach jaati hai.



5. API VERSIONING
------------------

API Gateway multiple API versions support kar sakta hai.

Example:

    /api/v1/users

    /api/v2/users


NOTE:

User Service V1 aur User Service V2 generally User Service ke
different deployed versions ko represent karte hain.

Har version ke multiple running instances ho sakte hain, aur
unhe manage karne ke liye us version ka apna Load Balancer
bhi ho sakta hai.

Request ke API version ke basis par API Gateway request ko
corresponding version ke Load Balancer tak route kar deta hai.

Example:

    /api/v1/users

            -> User Service V1 Load Balancer

    /api/v2/users

            -> User Service V2 Load Balancer

However, ye bhi possible hai ki V1 aur V2 APIs alag deployments
ki jagah same User Service ke andar hi different endpoints ke
through implement ki gayi hon.

Ye implementation architecture aur deployment strategy par
depend karta hai.



6. LOGGING
------------

Gateway har incoming request aur outgoing response ka
log maintain kar sakta hai.

Example Logged Data:

    Client IP
    HTTP Method
    URL
    Response Status
    Response Time
    Timestamp


7. MONITORING
---------------

Gateway operational metrics collect karke monitoring systems
(Prometheus, Grafana, CloudWatch etc.) ko bhej sakta hai.

Examples:

    Average Latency
    P95 / P99 Latency
    Requests per Second
    Error Rate
    CPU / Memory Metrics



8. REQUEST VALIDATION
-----------------------

Gateway basic request validation perform kar sakta hai.

Example:

Client Request:

{
    "email":""
}

Email mandatory hai.

Result:

    400 Bad Request

Invalid request service tak nahi jayegi.



9. REQUEST TRANSFORMATION
----------------------------

Gateway request ko modify ya enrich kar sakta hai
before forwarding it to the backend service.

Example:

Client sends:

{
    "name":"Anurag"
}

Gateway internally adds:

{
    "name":"Anurag",
    "country":"India",
    "requestId":"123"
}

Uske baad Gateway request ko corresponding backend service ke
Load Balancer ko forward karta hai, jo eventually request ko
service ke kisi healthy instance tak route kar deta hai.



10. RESPONSE TRANSFORMATION
----------------------------

Gateway backend response ko modify karke client ko bhej sakta hai.

Example:

Backend returns:

{
    "id":1,
    "name":"Anurag",
    "salary":100000
}

Gateway hides salary field.

Client receives:

{
    "id":1,
    "name":"Anurag"
}



11. SSL/TLS TERMINATION
------------------------

## WHAT IS SSL/TLS ?
----------------------

Suppose Client kisi website ko access karta hai.

Example:

    https://amazon.com

Dhyan do:

    HTTPS

Ye sirf HTTP protocol nahi hai.

HTTPS = HTTP + SSL/TLS

SSL (Secure Sockets Layer) and TLS (Transport Layer Security) are cryptographic protocols that encrypt data passed between a web browser and a server.
TLS is the modern, secure successor to SSL; original SSL is deprecated due to severe security flaws, though the term "SSL" remains widely used today.


## WITHOUT SSL/TLS:
-------------------

Client se bheja gaya data network me plain text me travel karega.

Example:

    Username = anurag
    Password = 123456

Agar koi attacker packets capture kar le,
to wo credentials dekh sakta hai.

With SSL/TLS:

Data encrypt hokar network me travel karta hai.

Example:

    J8SHD82JDJ29SKD...
    8DJ29DKS92KDJD...
    SKD92KDJD92KDJ...

Agar koi packets capture bhi kar le,
to actual data read nahi kar sakta.



## TLS HANDSHAKE :
-------------------

Sabse pehle Client aur Server ke beech ek process perform hoti hai,
jise TLS Handshake kaha jata hai.

Simplified Flow:

1. Client Server ko request bhejta hai aur bolta hai:

    "Main HTTPS connection establish karna chahta hu."

2. Server apna SSL/TLS Certificate Client ko bhejta hai.

3. Client certificate verify karta hai.

   Ye verify kiya jata hai ki:

   - Certificate valid hai ya nahi.
   - Certificate trusted Certificate Authority (CA)
     dwara issue kiya gaya hai ya nahi.
   - Client kisi fake ya malicious server se communicate
     to nahi kar raha.

4. Verification successful hone ke baad TLS Handshake complete hota hai.

5. TLS Handshake complete hone ke baad Client aur Server ke beech
   ek secure HTTPS connection establish ho jata hai.

   Ye connection encrypted hota hai, jiske through dono
   securely data exchange kar sakte hain.

6. Ab Client aur Server encrypted HTTP requests aur responses
   exchange karte hain.


## SSL/TLS TERMINATION :
------------------------

Suppose architecture kuch aisa hai:


                Client
                   |
                HTTPS
                   |
             API Gateway
                   |
             Backend Services


Client aur API Gateway ke beech TLS Handshake perform hota hai
(jaisa upar explain kiya gaya hai).

TLS Handshake successfully complete hone ke baad Client aur
API Gateway ke beech ek secure HTTPS connection establish ho jata hai.

Ab Client jo bhi HTTP request bhejta hai,
wo encrypted HTTPS request ke form me API Gateway tak pahunchti hai.

API Gateway us encrypted request ko decrypt karta hai.

Ye wahi point hai jahan Client aur API Gateway ke beech
TLS connection end (terminate) ho jata hai.


## WHY IS IT CALLED "TERMINATION"?
------------------------------------

Client aur API Gateway ke beech jo TLS connection establish hua tha,
wo API Gateway par end (terminate) ho jata hai.

Yahin par encrypted HTTPS request decrypt kar di jaati hai.

Isliye is process ko SSL/TLS Termination kaha jata hai.

Termination ke baad API Gateway request ko Backend Services tak

    HTTP

ya

    HTTPS

ke through forward kar sakta hai,

depending on the system architecture.

## QUESTION: "AGAR GATEWAY NE REQUEST DECRYPT KAR DI, TO BACKEND KO HTTPS KAISE BHEJEGA?"
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Decryption ke baad request plain HTTP form me Gateway ke paas hoti hai.
Agar architecture require karta hai, to Gateway backend ke saath ek naya TLS session establish karta hai, request ko dobara encrypt karta hai, aur HTTPS ke through forward karta hai.
Isliye Client-Gateway aur Gateway-Backend do independent TLS connections ho sakte hain.


## WHY DO SSL/TLS TERMINATION?
-------------------------------

Suppose system me 100 Backend Services hain.

Agar har Backend Service khud TLS Handshake perform kare,
to har service ko:

    - SSL/TLS Certificate maintain karna padega.
    - Certificate renew karna padega.
    - TLS Handshake perform karna padega.
    - Encryption / Decryption handle karna padega.

Ye management aur maintenance difficult bana deta hai.

Isliye production systems me commonly API Gateway,
Load Balancer perform karte hain.


## BENIFITS :
-------------
    - Centralized Certificate Management
    - Easier Certificate Renewal

## NOTE:
---------

Most modern API Gateway implementations support SSL/TLS termination.
However, SSL/TLS termination is an additional capability, not the primary responsibility of an API Gateway (Request Routing + Cross-cutting concerns (Authentication, Authorization, Rate Limiting, etc). 
In some architectures, SSL is terminated at a Load Balancer or another Reverse Proxy before the request reaches the API Gateway.



12. CIRCUIT BREAKING (Depending on Implementation)
----------------------------------------------------

Suppose koi downstream service (e.g. Payment Service)
repeatedly fail ho rahi hai.

Agar API Gateway har incoming request us service ko
forward karta rahe, to:

    - Unnecessary network calls hongi.
    - System resources waste honge.
    - Failing service par aur load padega.

Is situation me Circuit Breaker temporarily "Open"
ho jata hai.

Circuit Open hone ke baad Gateway us service ko
request forward nahi karta aur immediately client ko
appropriate fallback ya error response return kar deta hai.

Examples:

    503 Service Unavailable

                OR

    "Payment Service is temporarily unavailable.
     Please try again later."

Isse unnecessary requests aur cascading failures
avoid ho jaate hain.




13. LOAD BALANCING (Depending on Implementation)
-------------------------------------------------

Kuch API Gateway implementations backend service instances ke
beech khud bhi load balancing perform kar sakte hain.

Example:

                     API Gateway
                          |
           ---------------------------------
           |               |               |
           v               v               v
      User Instance-1  User Instance-2  User Instance-3

Gateway incoming requests ko available instances ke
beech distribute kar sakta hai.

NOTE:

Ye implementation par depend karta hai.

Production systems me commonly API Gateway ke baad
dedicated Service Load Balancers ya Service Discovery
mechanisms (Eureka, Consul, Kubernetes Services, etc.)
backend service instances ko discover aur load balance
karte hain.

Isliye har architecture me API Gateway khud load
balancing perform kare, ye zaruri nahi hai.


## IS A SINGLE API GATEWAY ENOUGH?
------------------------------------

Conceptually ek hi API Gateway sufficient ho sakta hai.

Architecture:

                    DNS
                     |
                     v
               API Gateway
                     |
      -----------------------------------------
      |                       |               |               
      v                       v               v               
  User Service LB      Order Service LB      Payment Service LB
      |                     |                      |
      v                     v                      v
 User Instances      Order Instances      Payment Instances


Ye architecture small applications, ya low traffic systems ke liye perfectly valid hai.

Lekin production environments me generally sirf ek API Gateway
par depend nahi kiya jata.

High traffic handle karne ke liye ise bhi horizontally scale karna padta hai.

Agar sirf ek API Gateway ho aur wo down ho jaye,to saari client requests fail ho jayengi.

Isliye production systems me generally multiple API Gateway instances deploy kiye jaate hain.

Ye Single Point of Failure (SPOF) create karta hai.



## PRODUCTION ARCHITECTURE
----------------------------

DNS resolution ke baad generally API gateway ke Load Balancer ka IP return hota hai.

Flow:

    User
      |
      v
    DNS
      |
      | returns Load Balancer IP
      v
    Load Balancer
      |
      |----------------------|----------------------|
      v                      v                      v
 API Gateway-1          API Gateway-2        API Gateway-3
      |                      |                      |
      |----------------------|----------------------|
                             |
      -----------------------------------------------
