Load Balancer incoming requests ko multiple API Gateway
instances ke beech distribute karta hai.

Agar koi ek API Gateway fail ho jaye,
to Load Balancer automatically remaining healthy API Gateway
instances ko traffic bhej deta hai.

Is approach se:

    - High Availability improve hoti hai.
    - Scalability improve hoti hai.
    - Single Point of Failure avoid hota hai.



14. COMPRESSION
-----------------

Compression ka matlab hota hai HTTP Request ya Response ke size ko
kam karna before transmitting it over the network.

Iska primary purpose hai:

    - Network bandwidth reduce karna jiski wajah se response fast milta hai usse Overall network performance improve hota hai.


## WITHOUT COMPRESSION
-----------------------

Suppose Backend Service response return karti hai:

    500 KB JSON

Flow:

        Backend service
           |
        500 KB
           |
        Service LB
           |
        API Gateway
           |
        Internet
           |
         Client


Poora 500 KB network ke through transfer hoga.


## WITH COMPRESSION
--------------------

API Gateway response ko GZIP ya Brotli jaise compression
algorithms use karke compress kar sakta hai.

Example:

        Backend Service
           |
        500 KB JSON
           |
        Service LB
           |
      API Gateway (GZIP / Brotli)
           |
         50 KB
           |
        Internet
           |
         Client


Client ka Browser ya HTTP Client automatically compressed
response ko decompress kar deta hai.

Application Developer ko manually decompression
karne ki zarurat nahi padti.


## COMMONLY COMPRESSED CONTENT
-------------------------------

- JSON
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- XML
- Text Responses


## COMMONLY NOT COMPRESSED
---------------------------

Already compressed files ko generally dubara compress
nahi kiya jata.

Examples:

- JPEG
- PNG
- MP4
- ZIP
- PDF (mostly)


## COMMON COMPRESSION ALGORITHMS
--------------------------------

- GZIP (Most Common)

- Brotli (Better Compression, Modern Browsers)


