CASE 5: MICROSERVICES ARCHITECTURE WITH A LAYER-7 LOAD BALANCER (WITHOUT A DEDICATED API GATEWAY)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose ek microservices architecture hai jisme multiple services hain.

Example:

    User Service
    Order Service
    Payment Service

Har service ke multiple instances different servers par run kar rahe hain.

In services ke traffic ko handle karne ke liye ek Layer-7
(Application Layer) Load Balancer use kiya ja raha hai.

Ye Load Balancer URL / Path based routing support karta hai.

Is architecture me separate API Gateway mandatory nahi hai.

Relatively simple applications me Layer-7 Load Balancer
khud hi incoming requests ko appropriate backend service
tak route kar sakta hai.


Example Routing Rules:

    /users/**

            -> User Service

    /orders/**

            -> Order Service

    /payments/**

            -> Payment Service

  
Layer-7 Load Balancer pehle incoming request ka URL
check karta hai aur determine karta hai ki request
kis service ko bhejni hai.

Uske baad woh us service ke available instances me se
kisi ek healthy instance ko select karta hai using
load balancing algorithms like:

    - Round Robin
    - Least Connections
    - Weighted Routing
    etc.



## FLOW :
----------

                User
                  |
                  v
                 DNS
                  |
                  | returns CDN IP
                  v
            Nearby CDN Edge
                  |
                  | Cache Miss
                  v
          Layer-7 Load Balancer
                  |
      -----------------------------------------
      |                  |                    |
      |                  |                    |
      v                  v                    v

  User Target Group  Order Target Group  Payment Target Group

      |                  |                    |
  ----------        ----------            ----------
   User-1            Order-1              Payment-1
   User-2            Order-2              Payment-2
   User-3            Order-3              Payment-3




## LIMITATIONS :
----------------

Compared to a dedicated API Gateway,
a Layer-7 Load Balancer generally provides limited support
for advanced API management features such as:

    - Authentication
    - Authorization
    - Rate Limiting
    - API Versioning
    - Request Transformation
    - Response Transformation etc.

Exact capabilities Load Balancer implementation
par depend karti hain.

## COMMON EXAMPLES OF LAYER-7 LOAD BALANCERS
---------------------------------------------

Software Layer-7 Load Balancers

    - NGINX
    - HAProxy
    - Traefik
    - Envoy

Cloud Managed Layer-7 Load Balancers

    - AWS Application Load Balancer (ALB)
    - Azure Application Gateway
    - Google Cloud HTTP(S) Load Balancer


