## WHAT IS PROXY ?
======================

Proxy = Middleman (Intermediate Server)

Yaani Client aur Actual Server ke beech ek aur server aa jata hai.

Proxy ek intermediate server hota hai jo Client aur Actual Server ke beech baithkar requests aur responses ko forward karta hai.

Instead of:

Client
   |
   |
Server

It becomes:

Client
   |
Proxy
   |
Server

## TYPES OF PROXY :
-------------------

1. FORWARD PROXY
-----------------

Forward Proxy client ko represent karta hai, i.e. wo client ki taraf se destination server se communicate karta hai 

Jab bhi Client koi request bhejta hai, wo request pehle Forward Proxy ke paas jaati hai. Forward Proxy us request ko Actual Server tak forward karta hai. Isliye server ko request Forward Proxy se aati hui dikhti hai, actual client se nahi.

Server request ko process karta hai aur response wapas Forward Proxy ko bhejta hai. Uske baad Forward Proxy response ko Client tak forward kar deta hai.

Flow:

Client
   |
Forward Proxy
   |
Actual Server


## IMPORTANT :
--------------

Forward Proxy client-side concerns jaise Filtering, Access Control aur Anonymity handle karta hai.

By default, server ko client ka original IP ya identity pata nahi hoti. Ye information tabhi pata chalti hai jab Forward Proxy intentionally usse forward kare (e.g. through HTTP headers like X-Forwarded-For).


USE CASE 1: CORPORATE INTERNET ACCESS CONTROL
-----------------------------------------------

Problem :

Suppose ek company (e.g. SCB) nahi chahti ki employees office network se Facebook, Instagram ya malicious websites access karein.

Agar employees directly Internet access karein:

Employee Laptop
       |
       |
   Internet

To company ke paas Internet usage ko centrally control karne ka koi mechanism nahi hoga.

Solution :

Company beech me ek Forward Proxy deploy karti hai.

Employee Laptop
       |
       |
Forward Proxy
       |
       |
   Internet

Ab har request pehle Forward Proxy ke paas jaati hai.

Example:

Employee requests:

facebook.com

Forward Proxy apni configured security policies check karta hai.

Rule:

facebook.com = BLOCKED

Result:

403 Forbidden

Request Facebook tak jaati hi nahi.

Agar employee StackOverflow access kare:

stackoverflow.com

Aur policy usse allow karti hai, to Forward Proxy request Internet par forward kar deta hai.

Benefits :

Centralized Internet Access Control
Website Filtering
Security Enforcement
Malware Protection
Logging & Monitoring


USE CASE 2: MASKING CLIENT IDENTITY (SIMPLIFIED)
-------------------------------------------------

Suppose Laptop ka private IP hai:

192.168.1.5

Router NAT/PAT ke through ise apne Public IP me convert karta hai:

49.205.10.20

## WITHOUT  FORWARD PROXY :

Laptop (192.168.1.5)
        |
Router (Public IP: 49.205.10.20)
        |
      Google


Google ko Router ka Public IP dikhega: 49.205.10.20

## WITH FORWARD PROXY :

Laptop
   |
Router (Public IP: 49.205.10.20)
   |
Forward Proxy (Public IP: 103.21.50.10)
   |
Google

Ab Google ko Forward Proxy ka Public IP dikhega:

103.21.50.10

Original Client ki identity ya Router ka Public IP tabhi pata chalega jab Forward Proxy intentionally us information ko forward kare (for example, through HTTP headers like X-Forwarded-For).


2. REVERSE PROXY
-----------------

Reverse Proxy server ko represent karta hai, i.e. wo server ki taraf se client se communicate karta hai.

In other words,

Jo bhi component Backend Server(s) ki taraf se Client ki requests receive karta hai aur Backend Infrastructure ko Client se hide karta hai, wo Reverse Proxy hai.

Ye Client aur Backend Servers ke beech ek intermediate server hota hai.


                  Client
                    |
              Reverse Proxy
                    |
               Backend Server(s)


Depending on the implementation, a Reverse Proxy can also act as:

    - Load Balancer
    - API Gateway
    - CDN
    - Ingress Controller


## NOTE :
-----------

NGINX (pronounced: Engine-X) is one of the most popular software implementations
that performs the role of a Reverse Proxy.

Ye Physical Server, Virtual Machine ya Container par run karta hai.

Configuration ke basis par NGINX different networking roles
perform kar sakta hai.

- Load Balancer
- Basic API Gateway
- Static File Server

Additionally, it supports features such as:

- SSL/TLS Termination
- Caching
- Compression


